## Appendix E: Alignment with UN Sustainable Development Goals

The [Roddenberry Foundation's 2024 Prize](https://roddenberryprize.org/) awarded $1 million to an early-stage AI venture aligned with the [UN Sustainable Development Goals](https://sdgs.un.org/goals). The Skills in this book map to the following SDGs (official UN titles used verbatim):


| SDG | Relevant Skills in This Book |
|---|---|
| *SDG 1* No Poverty | M-2 (credit card debt), M-4 (collections and bankruptcy), L-7 (debt collectors), W-2 (leaving a job and severance), L-10 and Li-3 (consumer protection and scams), Ho-5 (utility assistance and weatherization) |
| *SDG 3* Good Health and Well-Being | The Health domain (H-1 through H-18), H-8 and Li-8 (wellness and nutrition), Ch-4 and Ch-6 (cooking and meal planning) |
| *SDG 4* Quality Education | M-9 (financial aid and student loans), Li-10 (language learning), Li-13 (public and academic libraries), WB-1 (learning any digital skill), Cr-10 (learning an instrument) |
| *SDG 5* Gender Equality | L-6 (family court), W-3 and W-9 (HR and workplace conflict, including discrimination complaints), Li-7 (raising kids) |
| *SDG 7* Affordable and Clean Energy | Ho-5 (utility bills and energy options), Tr-9 (electric vehicles), Tr-3 (transit, cycling, and walkability) |
| *SDG 10* Reduced Inequalities | The Legal domain (L-1 through L-10), C-1 through C-3 (police encounters, voter rights, rights where you live), H-6b (Medicaid), Tr-8 (accessible transportation) |
| *SDG 11* Sustainable Cities and Communities | The Home domain (Ho-1 through Ho-10), C-4 through C-6 (ballot measures, public comment, advocating for change), Tr-3 (transit and walkability) |
| *SDG 13* Climate Action | Ho-5 (energy options), Tr-9 (electric vehicles), Tr-3 (transit), Ch-1 (shopping your values) |
| *SDG 16* Peace, Justice, and Strong Institutions | The Legal domain (L-1 through L-10), the Civic domain (C-1 through C-8), IRL-1 (navigating government offices) |
| *SDG 17* Partnerships for the Goals | Chapter 34 (teaching this to someone you love — network effects of access) |
